.TH baseline 1  "baseline " 
.SH NAME
baseline \- Manage the accepted\-debt baseline (directive §16)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbaseline\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the accepted\-debt baseline (directive §16)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
baseline\-create(1)
Record every current finding as accepted debt. From then on, `sleak check` only blocks on *new* findings not already in the baseline — a project doesn\*(Aqt need to reach zero findings before Sleak becomes useful as a gate
.TP
baseline\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
